---
source: bin/tests/shell_idiom.rs
---
stdenv.mkDerivation { installPhase = ''
  runHook "preInstall"
  cp ${src} dst; chown ${owner} dst; chmod 755 dst
  cp src existingDir; chmod 700 existingDir
  cat Cargo.toml | read value
  rm -f dst && ln -s src dst
  runHook "postInstall"
''; }
---
<temp_file_path>>5:20:I:28:[shellcheck] SC2162: read without -r will mangle backslashes.
<temp_file_path>>3:3:I:33:[shell_idiom] `cp` + `chown` + `chmod` can be one `install`
<temp_file_path>>4:3:I:33:[shell_idiom] `cp` + `chmod` can be one `install`
<temp_file_path>>5:3:I:33:[shell_idiom] `cat` only feeds `read`: read the file directly
<temp_file_path>>6:3:I:33:[shell_idiom] `rm -f` then `ln -s`: `ln -sfn` replaces the link
